{"item_id":"E-RES-609","ledger":[{"claim_id":"Q01","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The intended reader is an owner-operator of a 1–10 person small business"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI fits"},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a measurable outcome"}],"rationale":"This is a planned instruction to reframe the abstract topic as a bounded workflow decision and to test AI suitability; it asserts no current implementation or observed result. The approach is consistent with the diagnostic model in approved evidence.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed as a framing/diagnostic step. Confine the candidate tasks to general small-business workflows (document, email, CRM, back-office) and state honestly that AI may not fit; do not imply Bareni has automated invoicing or collections for anyone."},{"claim_id":"Q02","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The representative pains are 8–10 hours a week of repeated customer questions, neglected sales leads, and manual invoice/data work."},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The 8–10 hours is a persona scenario, not a market statistic or observed customer result."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Keep observed results, estimates, targets, synthetic data, and examples distinct."}],"rationale":"Approved evidence supports manual invoice/data work as a representative pain, so naming an operational gap is permissible; but the claim as written presents the mechanism generically and the specific gaps (manual invoice tracking, chasing emails, spreadsheet aging reports) are not in the evidence as observed facts.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that any named gap is an illustrative persona example, not an observed customer situation or measured cash-flow effect; label it as an example and avoid any figure or claim of typical impact."},{"claim_id":"Q03","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C01","quote":"a six-person D2C online shop whose owner compares an automation investment with the cost of another hire"},{"source_id":"S01","quote":"the owner compares a bounded automation investment with continuing
  manual work or hiring; final approval and business authority remain human"}],"rationale":"The comparison between automation, hiring and continuing manual work is supported as the persona's decision context, but the claim presents it as a comparison owners 'already face' without marking it as the representative persona scenario rather than a researched market fact.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that this is the representative persona decision context, not a surveyed or observed customer pattern; keep the framing neutral and non-sales, and note that final approval stays with the owner."},{"claim_id":"Q04","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Normal sequence: free 30-minute diagnostic; free one-page pilot proposal;
  paid working MVP in days; fixed-price pilot in weeks"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Timings are intended scopes, not guarantees."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI
  fits, and—if it does—defines pilot scope, fixed price, and measures."}],"rationale":"The diagnostic purpose and the sequence are supported, but the claim omits that stated timings are intended scopes rather than guarantees, and that the diagnostic may conclude AI does not fit.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that timings are intended scopes, not guarantees, and that the diagnostic can honestly conclude AI is not suitable. Describe the sequence as policy only; per the CTA rule, do not turn the free diagnostic mention into an invitation to book."},{"claim_id":"Q05","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"explain one observable workflow decision, threshold, diagnostic question,
  control, or next step"},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a measurable outcome"}],"rationale":"This supplies a self-directed diagnostic question for the reader; it asserts no current fact, capability or observed hours and matches the persona's requirement for one observable diagnostic step.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed as a question the reader answers for themselves. Do not attach any hour figure as typical or observed, and keep it free of any booking prompt."},{"claim_id":"Q06","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"CTA: use none unless the task explicitly authorises one."},{"source_id":"S01","quote":"**CTA rule:** None."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Informational posts use no CTA or one soft closing sentence."}],"rationale":"This is an instruction about how to close the post with a neutral practical note instead of a CTA; it is a permissible plan, not a factual assertion about Bareni.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed. Ensure the close is a neutral next-step observation only — no meeting invitation, no offer to discuss, no scarcity or capacity framing — and hold to plain founder-to-founder voice with at most one understated aside."}]}

